  "title": "ACB seeks 14-day judicial custody of Satyendar Jain and others in Delhi Jal Board case",
  "summary": "The Anti-Corruption Branch (ACB) has sought 14 days of judicial custody of former Delhi minister Satyendar Jain and ex-Delhi Jal Board CEO Udit Prakash Rai, along with three others, over alleged corruption, irregularities, and money laundering linked to a sewage treatment plant project tender. The ACB also sought the police custody of only one of the six accused, Ankit Srivastava, a former contractual consultant.",
